//? Title: Floating Newton division
//? Subtitle: Actual normalized reciprocal steps, exponent-safe rescaling and finite controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Approximate a floating quotient using a scaled reciprocal-Newton iteration
followed by multiplication. Actual native operands expose the seed and stopping
behavior, while the original four signed examples and six-step reciprocal
diagnostic are retained. A real100000-pair comparison replaces an unsupported
old verification claim, and full-exponent controls expose why quotient scaling
must avoid an overflowing intermediate reciprocal.
)

\toc

> Normalize the divisor, then refine its reciprocal

Write abs(D)=m_D·2^e_D with m_D in[.5,1). The fixed seed x0=48/17−(32/17)m_D
targets1/m_D. For exact arithmetic, e=1−m_D x transforms under x_next=x(2−m_D x)
into e_next=e². On the normalized interval the seed’s maximum absolute relative
residual is1/17: its endpoint residuals are1/17 and its midpoint residual
is−1/17. Squaring explains local rapid improvement, while floating updates
eventually stagnate or oscillate rather than doubling correct digits forever.

The actual shared update records its rounded product m_D*x, factor2-product and
assigned x*factor. Fused residuals fma(−m_D,x,1) are separate diagnostics, not
hidden update operands. Their smaller cancellation error does not turn them into
certified real-arithmetic error bounds.

> A hand-checkable first normalized step for division by3

For D=3, frexp gives m_D=.75 and e_D=2. The seed is24/17; the first
exact-arithmetic update would be384/289, with residual1/289. The figure reads
the actual rounded native seed, product, factor and assigned reciprocal from a
real division trace. Its output quotient is formed only after the normalized
reciprocal loop ends.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newton_division_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newton_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::newton_division_trace(1, 3);
    auto s = t.steps.front();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("seed", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual normalized D={}\nseed {:.10f}",
                       t.run.denominator_mantissa, s.before));
    d.node("factor", {7, 0},
           std::format("Actual product {:.10f}\nfactor {:.10f}", s.product,
                       s.factor));
    d.node("next", {14, 0},
           std::format("Actual next {:.10f}\nfused residual {:.10f}", s.after,
                       s.residual_after));
    d.edge("seed", "factor").edge("factor", "next");
    std::print("Actual denominator exponent {}; actual first normalized reciprocal {}.\n",
               t.run.denominator_exponent, s.after);
    d.save_svg("build/newton_division_tiny.svg");
}
```
