> Retain the original four signed division pairs

The original examples are1/3,−7/1024,5/10⁻⁹ and22/7. The table compares actual
canonical quotients with built-in double division. The producer retains the old
relative state-change stopping test abs(next−before)<=10⁻¹⁷·abs(next), with at
most60 updates. That threshold is below typical relative double spacing, so
exact stationarity often causes the stop; a small oscillation can exhaust the
cap. A finite returned quotient is an approximation, not a correctly-rounded
division guarantee.

The actual driver history for division by3 is plotted below. “Residual digits”
means−log10(max(abs(fused residual),10⁻¹⁸)); the display floor is explicit. It
is not an extra iteration, a timing measurement or a proof of a corresponding
number of correct quotient digits.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newton_division_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newton_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::print("| numerator | denominator | actual native quotient | built-in comparison | actual updates | " "stationary stop |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto[n, d] : dm::algorithms::newton_division_demo_pairs()) {
        auto r = dm::algorithms::newton_division_run(n, d);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, d, r.quotient, n / d,
                   r.updates, r.stationary);
    }
    auto t = dm::algorithms::newton_division_trace(1, 3);
    std::vector<double> x{0}, digits{-std::log10(std::max(
                                                 std::abs(
                                                 t.steps.front().residual_before),
                                                 1e-18))};
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        digits.push_back(-std::log10(std::max(std::abs(t.steps[i].residual_after),
                                              1e-18)));
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(x, digits, "actual residual", {36, 105, 172}).points(x, digits, "",
                                                                 {36, 105, 172},
                                                                 5).title(
        "Actual floating-division reciprocal history for D=3").x_label(
        "actual completed updates").y_label("-log10(max(abs(fused residual), 1e-18))").save_svg("build/newton_division_original.svg");
}
```
