> Preserve the fixed six-update diagnostic and perform the claimed comparison

The old report also ran exactly six reciprocal updates regardless of the
division driver’s stop. That separate educational experiment is retained through
the native fixed-update API, with the same normalized divisor and seed. Its
table includes stationary updates instead of pretending the driver requested
them. The exact-arithmetic error-squaring identity remains distinct from
measured floating residuals.

The original text claimed verification over100000 random pairs without actually
executing that study in its report program. The canonical check now generates
and evaluates those pairs. A local MT19937_64 seed7 supplies signed mantissas
and exponents−500..500 in a fixed draw order, ensuring finite nonzero reference
quotients. The plot shows sampled maximum relative differences from built-in
division in units of machine epsilon for increasing prefix budgets. This
observed finite-sample comparison is not a universal accuracy bound or an
independent correctly-rounded oracle.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/newton_division_check.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/newton_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto driver = dm::algorithms::newton_division_run(1, 3);
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::newton_reciprocal_trace(driver.denominator_mantissa,
                                                driver.seed, 6);
    std::print("| completed fixed updates | actual reciprocal | actual fused residual |\n| ---: | ---: | " "---: |\n| 0 | {} | {} |\n",
               t.seed, t.initial_residual);
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", i + 1, t.steps[i].after,
                   t.steps[i].residual_after);
    std::vector<double> x, error;
    std::print("\n| sampled pairs | actual maximum relative difference | first worst index |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t count : {10, 100, 1000, 10000, 100000}) {
        auto c = dm::algorithms::newton_division_check(count, 7);
        x.push_back(count);
        error.push_back(c.max_relative_error / std::numeric_limits<double>::epsilon());
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", c.checked, c.max_relative_error,
                   c.worst_index);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, error, "sampled maximum", {192, 59, 50}, 5).title(
        "Actual seeded comparison with built-in floating division").x_label(
        "sampled pairs").y_label("maximum relative difference / machine epsilon").save_svg("build/newton_division_check.svg");
}
```
