| --- | ---: | ---: | --- | --- | --- | ---: |
| sub/sub | 1 | 1 | false | false | false | 5 |
| min/sub | 4503599627370496 | 4503599627370496 | false | false | false | 5 |
| max/max | 0.9999999999999999 | 1 | false | false | false | 5 |
| underflow | -0 | -0 | true | false | true | 5 |
| zero | -0 | -0 | true | true | false | 0 |
\image(figures/newton_division_controls.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual reciprocal work for finite full-exponent and signed-zero controls.)
\alttext(Equal subnormals produce1 without an overflowing raw reciprocal; underflow and the zero shortcut remain explicit in the computed table.)

> Contracts and interpretation

Both operands must be finite and the denominator nonzero, with complete checks
before arithmetic or history policies. Nonfinite updates or a nonfinite final
quotient throw; finite gradual underflow and signed zero are retained. The
ordinary routine has at most60 updates and constant driver storage. Actual
division trace units are3+updates, with default1000000 and zero disabling the
quota; admission precedes each recorded update. The fixed educational trace
instead pre-admits4+requested_updates. Neither count is a byte or peak-memory
claim.

The update itself uses multiplications and subtraction, but seed constants,
exponent operations, compiler lowering and the complete call are not asserted to
form a division-free hardware instruction stream. No timing or constant-time
conclusion follows from these counters. The algebraic derivation, actual update
records and extreme-scale controls specify what this implementation computes,
while the sampled comparison remains a finite empirical check.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes75 CTest cases,22 directly instrumented ASan/UBSan
cases,122 compiled and executed public examples,538/538 scoped documentation
definitions and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
arbitrary-precision arithmetic verifies69365 captured division records
with656460 checks; native independent polynomial, geometry, finite-range, graph,
ranking and callback checks cover the remaining producers. Frozen valid-input
comparisons preserve Neville recurrences, Newton result/callback paths, complete
byte encodings, switch routes and NSGA-II complete objective-call
sequences/final fronts. Ten checkout headers and ten byte-identical installed
development headers compile independently; an installed-header native consumer
links and runs. All40 complete programs execute, and40 native figures have been
visually reviewed; HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed rows/prose and
identical image bytes. Checks are scoped native checks, not an installation
claim for every language binding. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-254-263/`.
